The tagger's model: MASC (American National Corpus)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The web edition's lexical-class tagger (FRUSLanguage) is an averaged perceptron
whose weights were trained, by this repository's frus-language tool, from the
part-of-speech annotations of MASC 3.0.0, the Manually Annotated Sub-Corpus of
the American National Corpus (https://anc.org/data/masc/), its written genres,
with MASC's Penn Treebank syntax. MASC is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 3.0 United States License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/). The model, compiled into the
server's binary and committed as Sources/FRUSLanguage/EmbeddedModel.swift with
its provenance, is a work derived from those annotations; MASC's texts and
annotations themselves are not part of the image or of this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WordNet 3.0 (Princeton University)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The tagger's lemmatizer reads WordNet 3.0's exception lists and the single
words of its indexes, compiled into the server's binary and committed as
Sources/FRUSLanguage/EmbeddedWordNet.swift. Its licence follows.

